WEBVTT

00:14.710 --> 00:19.070
<b><i>A "friendly" sightseeing trip is our 
answer to Ildoa's breach of trust.</i></b>

00:19.070 --> 00:20.850
<b><i>The goal, honestly, is intimidation.</i></b>

00:20.850 --> 00:23.780
<b><i>But it's a better, easier way to do it 
that won't get anybody killed.</i></b>

00:30.210 --> 00:32.500
<b><i>Well-starched sleeves.</i></b>

00:32.800 --> 00:34.960
<b><i>Properly polished boots.</i></b>

00:34.960 --> 00:37.310
<b><i>Beautifully folded collars.</i></b>

00:37.310 --> 00:41.180
<b><i>It's been a long time since I've seen 
uniforms in condition this good.</i></b>

00:41.670 --> 00:46.590
<b><i>But now they're all rudely staring 
at my short stature.</i></b>

00:53.730 --> 00:54.950
<b><i>Why?</i></b>

00:54.950 --> 00:58.150
<b><i>The sky is so clear...</i></b>

00:58.950 --> 01:00.620
<b><i>But I just can't relax.</i></b>

01:00.620 --> 01:04.290
<b><i>Why do I feel so uncomfortable?</i></b>

02:36.050 --> 02:41.970
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:44.940 --> 02:46.290
<b>Excuse me.</b>

02:51.420 --> 02:54.170
<b><i>If he sets it there, 
the vibrations will...</i></b>

02:54.990 --> 02:56.320
<b><i>It's not shaking?</i></b>

02:57.550 --> 03:00.100
<b><i>This would never happen in the Empire.</i></b>

03:00.100 --> 03:02.740
<b><i>Their rails are that much 
better-maintained than ours?</i></b>

03:04.050 --> 03:06.780
<b><i>I guess a peace dividend is a big thing.</i></b>

03:07.250 --> 03:10.870
<b><i>Hooray for peace. I'm quite jealous.</i></b>

03:11.500 --> 03:14.500
<b>Episode Nine
Sightseeing Tour</b>

03:16.180 --> 03:18.070
<b><i>The greatest bread of them all!</i></b>

03:18.070 --> 03:21.430
<b><i>One made from refined white flour!</i></b>

03:21.670 --> 03:25.740
<b><i>In the imperial capital, 
they ration the damn K-brot!</i></b>

03:26.140 --> 03:28.070
<b><i>Is Colonel Calandro here yet?</i></b>

03:28.070 --> 03:32.300
<b><i>He's a monster, forcing me to 
stare at this food and not eat it!</i></b>

03:41.900 --> 03:43.570
<b>Lt. Colonel Degurechaff.</b>

03:43.570 --> 03:45.290
<b>Oh, Colonel!</b>

03:45.890 --> 03:48.290
<b>Sorry to keep you waiting.</b>

03:48.290 --> 03:53.590
<b>The military brass was trying to 
fill your day with welcome parties.</b>

03:53.590 --> 03:56.880
<b>I had no idea we were so popular.</b>

03:56.880 --> 04:00.550
<b>You'd spend the day deepening our
friendship instead of letting us outside?</b>

04:00.550 --> 04:04.360
<b>Don't worry. I've prepared 
a much better day for you.</b>

04:04.360 --> 04:06.170
<b>You were quite kind to me in the east.</b>

04:06.170 --> 04:10.610
<b>I promise that you'll have a valuable, 
peaceful trip, without restrictions.</b>

04:10.610 --> 04:16.070
<b>I can tell your words 
are implying quite a lot.</b>

04:16.070 --> 04:23.080
<b>The gentle sun here can make you 
a poet, an orator, or a musician.</b>

04:24.060 --> 04:28.240
<b>And it's not just the people who love 
the sun. Ildoa's greenery loves it too.</b>

04:28.700 --> 04:33.720
<b>The lemons that spend their days in 
the sun, the fragrant blood oranges,</b>

04:33.720 --> 04:35.590
<b>all contain our country's history.</b>

04:35.590 --> 04:36.860
<b><i>Enough!</i></b>

04:36.860 --> 04:38.410
<b><i>Can we eat yet?</i></b>

04:43.850 --> 04:46.590
<b>Now, let's have a welcome lunch.</b>

04:46.590 --> 04:48.970
<b>What do you want? Any preferences?</b>

04:48.970 --> 04:50.750
<b>Let me see the menu.</b>

04:52.710 --> 04:56.180
<b><i>A cafeteria car gets this many options?</i></b>

04:56.740 --> 05:00.180
<b><i>In the Imperial Capital, 
you've got one choice: war sausage.</i></b>

05:00.680 --> 05:03.860
<b>I recommend the seafood, by the way.</b>

05:03.860 --> 05:06.240
<b>It's not what you'd usually choose 
for a multi-course meal,</b>

05:06.240 --> 05:09.080
<b>but this place has a better selection 
than your average port.</b>

05:09.080 --> 05:11.740
<b>The really good fish is rare.</b>

05:11.740 --> 05:14.230
<b>You should take this opportunity 
to enjoy them while you can.</b>

05:15.010 --> 05:19.790
<b>All right, then, 
I'll have this marinated fish.</b>

05:20.830 --> 05:22.640
<b>A wonderful choice.</b>

05:22.990 --> 05:26.550
<b>Oh, I'm also quite hopeful 
for the initial skirmish...</b>

05:26.840 --> 05:29.690
<b>Oh, you mean an appetizer?</b>

05:29.690 --> 05:32.420
<b>How about a light steak tartare?</b>

05:32.420 --> 05:34.920
<b>It might not be what 
you're used to in the Empire,</b>

05:34.920 --> 05:36.940
<b>but we're quite proud of our beef.</b>

05:37.240 --> 05:38.890
<b>All right, I'll try it.</b>

05:39.300 --> 05:45.410
<b><i>Now, let me see if you 
can back up your words.</i></b>

05:56.040 --> 05:59.470
<b>I look forward to hearing what you think.</b>

06:04.640 --> 06:06.800
<b><i>It looks simple at first glance, but...</i></b>

06:12.320 --> 06:13.460
<b><i>It's so good!</i></b>

06:13.460 --> 06:16.440
<b><i>The flavor is so rich, I can't stand it!</i></b>

06:16.440 --> 06:20.340
<b><i>This light touch of spice 
that brings out the flavor of the meat...</i></b>

06:20.340 --> 06:23.270
<b><i>It's nothing like the usual trick 
you see with bad tartare,</i></b>

06:23.270 --> 06:25.400
<b><i>where they hide the raw flavor 
of the meat with pepper!</i></b>

06:25.400 --> 06:29.170
<b><i>My tongue's used to wurst made from 
scrap meat, so I'm about to pass out!</i></b>

06:29.170 --> 06:32.110
<b><i>Ildoa's meat is terrifyingly good!</i></b>

06:35.800 --> 06:39.550
<b><i>The appetizer was heavy, and now they're
following it up with a light potage...</i></b>

06:39.800 --> 06:44.700
<b><i>I can't help but have my doubts about 
this decision, but let's see...</i></b>

06:46.240 --> 06:49.330
<b><i>This refreshing sweetness and scent 
that races through my nose...</i></b>

06:49.330 --> 06:51.650
<b><i>Is this... zucchini?!</i></b>

06:51.650 --> 06:54.980
<b><i>Fresh early-summer vegetables,</i></b>

06:54.980 --> 06:58.270
<b><i>and a bouillon that's as 
flavorful as the tartare!</i></b>

06:58.520 --> 07:02.620
<b><i>The simplicity of the dish makes 
the skill of the chef all the more clear!</i></b>

07:08.530 --> 07:11.830
<b><i>And the mild sparkling water 
they offer between courses...</i></b>

07:11.830 --> 07:13.770
<b><i>My mouth is used to muddy water,</i></b>

07:13.770 --> 07:17.820
<b><i>so the sweetness of the 
minerals almost hurts!</i></b>

07:19.190 --> 07:21.960
<b>Now, it's time for the main course.</b>

07:23.260 --> 07:26.250
<b>Fresh, marinated fish is delicious.</b>

07:26.490 --> 07:30.790
<b>Though it might be a little much 
if you're not used to it.</b>

07:31.160 --> 07:34.440
<b><i>"Not used to it"? Hah!</i></b>

07:34.440 --> 07:36.680
<b><i>I'm Japanese, you know.</i></b>

07:36.680 --> 07:39.560
<b><i>I'm a harsh critic 
when it comes to fish dishes.</i></b>

07:51.480 --> 07:54.760
<b><i>There's something that goes beyond 
the flavor of the fish...</i></b>

07:54.760 --> 07:58.080
<b><i>It feels insulting to even 
attempt to express it in words.</i></b>

07:58.080 --> 08:01.100
<b><i>And the mild acidity of the sauce...</i></b>

08:02.650 --> 08:04.080
<b><i>I see...</i></b>

08:04.080 --> 08:07.080
<b><i>So this is the pride of Ildoa.</i></b>

08:16.850 --> 08:18.120
<b>Well?</b>

08:18.430 --> 08:21.350
<b>It seems you've taken a liking to it.</b>

08:21.670 --> 08:26.250
<b>For the first time in my life, 
the word "surrender" has crossed my mind.</b>

08:26.250 --> 08:27.500
<b>I have been utterly defeated.</b>

08:28.500 --> 08:31.510
<b>So we've driven the Empire's 
Silver Wings to surrender?</b>

08:31.510 --> 08:36.370
<b>You fight with guns, 
but our chefs fight with their knives.</b>

08:36.370 --> 08:39.160
<b>How very cultured.</b>

08:39.160 --> 08:44.460
<b>But I'm sure you enjoyed your taste of 
equality beneath the artillery guns.</b>

08:44.460 --> 08:47.970
<b>You're welcome back in 
our bunker anytime.</b>

08:48.260 --> 08:53.580
<b>Hmm. I'll remember that the next time 
we need to send an observer.</b>

08:54.360 --> 08:56.370
<b><i>An observer, huh?</i></b>

08:56.730 --> 09:02.810
<b><i>The words of someone who has no intention 
of being with us or against us.</i></b>

09:02.810 --> 09:05.650
<b><i>They think the great war 
has nothing to do with them?</i></b>

09:06.520 --> 09:10.150
<b><i>So they think they get to live in a 
peaceful, cultured, and rich world,</i></b>

09:10.150 --> 09:12.280
<b><i>and just watch the war unfold?</i></b>

09:13.360 --> 09:16.690
<b>Yeah... this pisses me off.</b>

09:18.700 --> 09:21.850
<b><i>Oh dear. I've forgotten myself.</i></b>

09:22.260 --> 09:26.180
<b><i>There's nothing so unproductive 
as being jealous of others.</i></b>

09:26.960 --> 09:33.090
<b>Ildoa Central Station</b>

09:38.460 --> 09:40.640
<b>The air feels so bright.</b>

09:40.640 --> 09:41.860
<b>What?</b>

09:42.380 --> 09:47.540
<b>A world with no debts to the departed, 
and no need to weep for the war dead...</b>

09:47.540 --> 09:48.550
<b>It's...</b>

09:51.520 --> 09:55.710
<b>Once again, welcome to our capital, 
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff.</b>

09:55.710 --> 09:59.690
<b>We welcome our allies and friends.</b>

10:03.910 --> 10:04.950
<b>What's this?</b>

10:04.950 --> 10:07.510
<b>Your ID and entry pass.</b>

10:07.510 --> 10:10.480
<b>And checks from Ildoa Strategic HQ.</b>

10:10.920 --> 10:14.770
<b>General Gassman was kind enough 
to pull them from some secret funds.</b>

10:15.240 --> 10:17.750
<b>You do have a spending limit, though.</b>

10:18.340 --> 10:24.020
<b><i>I could beg to my superiors and get 
nothing more than a few potatoes...</i></b>

10:24.390 --> 10:26.640
<b><i>I feel pathetic.</i></b>

10:26.640 --> 10:29.050
<b>Thank you for your kindness.</b>

10:29.050 --> 10:32.950
<b>I'm sure my unit is going to 
eat and drink quite a bit.</b>

10:32.950 --> 10:34.740
<b>Will that be all right?</b>

10:34.740 --> 10:36.380
<b>Of course.</b>

10:36.380 --> 10:39.900
<b>Unless you start gulping down 
airplane gasoline.</b>

10:40.570 --> 10:42.150
<b>Gasoline?</b>

10:42.150 --> 10:46.530
<b>Oh, you haven't heard this 
from Colonel Rerugen?</b>

10:46.530 --> 10:48.400
<b>The Empire is our ally.</b>

10:48.400 --> 10:53.240
<b>Given what we've heard 
about your fuel problems,</b>

10:53.240 --> 10:55.450
<b>of course we wanted to help.</b>

10:55.720 --> 11:00.310
<b>So instead of shedding blood 
with us, you'll shed fuel?</b>

11:00.790 --> 11:03.370
<b>I appreciate your kindness.</b>

11:03.370 --> 11:08.370
<b>If I get the chance, I'll make sure 
everyone is aware that you supported us.</b>

11:09.460 --> 11:11.010
<b>Please don't!</b>

11:11.010 --> 11:14.430
<b>Even if it's a well-known secret, 
it's still a secret!</b>

11:14.870 --> 11:18.390
<b>Does this support mean that 
the Empire's enemies will hate you,</b>

11:18.390 --> 11:20.730
<b>while the Imperial Army 
does little to thank you?</b>

11:20.950 --> 11:23.320
<b>It's our way of showing we're friends.</b>

11:23.320 --> 11:25.510
<b>We want to get along with you.</b>

11:25.510 --> 11:27.500
<b>I'm sorry we can't get more involved.</b>

11:27.900 --> 11:33.250
<b>They say that if you're nobody's enemy, 
you're also nobody's friend.</b>

11:33.250 --> 11:36.130
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, please don't say that.</b>

11:36.130 --> 11:39.000
<b>Ildoa is strictly neutral!</b>

11:39.000 --> 11:42.250
<b>We just want to be good neighbors!</b>

11:42.960 --> 11:45.420
<b><i>Ildoa is doing the right thing.</i></b>

11:45.420 --> 11:48.800
<b><i>If they can distance themselves 
from the war, they should.</i></b>

11:48.800 --> 11:51.030
<b><i>But the sad thing is...</i></b>

11:51.470 --> 11:55.070
<b><i>Even if they really don't want war...</i></b>

11:55.810 --> 11:58.410
<b><i>No, this is all a hypothesis, I guess.</i></b>

12:02.030 --> 12:04.570
<b><i>After that, we threw a huge party,</i></b>

12:04.570 --> 12:06.310
<b><i>we all got drunk,</i></b>

12:06.310 --> 12:10.110
<b><i>and our fun little trip 
in Ildoa came to an end.</i></b>

12:11.190 --> 12:15.490
<b><i>Of course, some of my men 
wanted to extend our stay.</i></b>

12:22.610 --> 12:25.210
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, what's wrong?</b>

12:26.090 --> 12:28.650
<b>Don't worry. It's nothing.</b>

12:30.230 --> 12:33.480
<b>But you seem depressed...</b>

12:33.480 --> 12:36.840
<b>No, I was just thinking 
about some things.</b>

12:39.870 --> 12:42.850
<b>The real stuff is good, isn't it?</b>

12:43.150 --> 12:45.110
<b>I bought a ton, too.</b>

12:45.110 --> 12:48.450
<b>I was using Ildoan money, 
so I didn't hold back.</b>

12:48.450 --> 12:52.740
<b>Ildoa gave me chocolate 
and refined sugar, too.</b>

12:53.060 --> 12:54.840
<b>I've got so many presents!</b>

12:55.350 --> 13:00.820
<b>I wish our Strategic HQ 
was as generous as theirs.</b>

13:00.820 --> 13:03.430
<b>Though I know that'll never happen.</b>

13:03.430 --> 13:06.340
<b>The food sure was good...</b>

13:07.040 --> 13:09.670
<b>And, well...</b>

13:10.290 --> 13:12.100
<b>It was so colorful.</b>

13:12.870 --> 13:14.890
<b>Yeah, you're right.</b>

13:17.680 --> 13:22.200
<b>By the way, Lieutenant, 
do you prefer white wine or red?</b>

13:22.820 --> 13:24.820
<b>Wine?</b>

13:24.820 --> 13:26.880
<b>I bought a few too many 
bottles to take home.</b>

13:26.880 --> 13:29.240
<b>Why not go share it with 
the other officers?</b>

13:29.240 --> 13:30.850
<b>You mean it?</b>

13:30.850 --> 13:32.200
<b>Thank you!</b>

13:39.640 --> 13:43.940
<b><i>So you can tell you're over the border 
from the way the rails start to creak?</i></b>

13:43.940 --> 13:47.850
<b><i>Both our countries are in the same world, 
but they're so different.</i></b>

13:49.910 --> 13:53.770
<b><i>Maybe it really is time to 
think about what comes next.</i></b>

14:01.230 --> 14:07.240
<b>July 3rd, Unified Year 1927, Imperial Capital</b>

14:07.950 --> 14:10.480
<b><i>And while I'm thinking about 
what comes next...</i></b>

14:10.480 --> 14:16.650
<b><i>I still need to write my report on 
the V-2 and what I saw in Ildoa!</i></b>

14:16.980 --> 14:19.000
<b><i>And while I'm thinking about 
what comes next...</i></b>

14:19.420 --> 14:21.260
<b><i>I still have to live my daily life.</i></b>

14:21.260 --> 14:23.420
<b><i>As a member of a large organization,</i></b>

14:23.420 --> 14:25.840
<b><i>making the rounds to say hello 
and give gifts is crucial.</i></b>

14:26.710 --> 14:30.590
<b>Huh? Captain Meybert and 
Lieutenant Tospan were arrested?</b>

14:30.590 --> 14:33.280
<b>They've since been freed, actually...</b>

14:33.280 --> 14:36.360
<b>This happened while you were gone.</b>

14:35.350 --> 14:38.100
<b>Western Empire Military Port</b>

14:38.280 --> 14:40.610
<b>At least give me permission 
to fire a warning shot!</b>

14:40.610 --> 14:43.540
<b>If they get close, we can't deal 
with them with artillery alone!</b>

14:43.540 --> 14:46.960
<b><i>Wait! We're verifying 
their affiliation now!</i></b>

14:46.960 --> 14:47.920
<b><i>Don't be reckless.</i></b>

14:47.920 --> 14:48.780
<b>Captain!</b>

14:48.780 --> 14:50.360
<b>Mages have taken off from their ships!</b>

14:50.360 --> 14:52.520
<b>They're approaching fast 
in assault formation!</b>

14:52.520 --> 14:53.520
<b>It's the enemy!</b>

14:53.760 --> 14:56.300
<b>This is what I was talking about!</b>

14:56.300 --> 14:58.380
<b>Lieutenant Tospan,
where are our allied mages?</b>

14:58.380 --> 14:59.630
<b>They're not out there!</b>

14:59.630 --> 15:01.580
<b>Our defenses are...</b>

15:01.580 --> 15:02.850
<b>Damn it!</b>

15:02.850 --> 15:04.540
<b>Stop preparing the artillery!</b>

15:04.540 --> 15:06.080
<b>Prepare for close-range combat!</b>

15:09.160 --> 15:11.860
<b><i>Artillery! Why aren't you firing?</i></b>

15:11.860 --> 15:13.720
<b><i>Don't let the enemy ships get close!</i></b>

15:14.930 --> 15:16.260
<b>We've lost communications!</b>

15:16.260 --> 15:17.980
<b>We will make decisions on our own!</b>

15:17.980 --> 15:19.560
<b>Continue close-range combat!</b>

15:20.080 --> 15:22.870
<b>So my men suggested a precaution 
that they ignored,</b>

15:22.870 --> 15:26.700
<b>and then they started complaining after 
my men acted to protect themselves.</b>

15:26.700 --> 15:31.300
<b>I thought the job of a soldier 
was to deal with reality, but...</b>

15:31.300 --> 15:35.750
<b>I never thought it was to play along 
with someone else's fantasies.</b>

15:36.210 --> 15:39.150
<b>You've every right to be upset.</b>

15:39.150 --> 15:41.450
<b>This is ridiculous and cannot be allowed.</b>

15:41.450 --> 15:44.960
<b>I've already talked to military 
police HQ and had them freed.</b>

15:44.960 --> 15:46.840
<b>Thank you.</b>

15:46.840 --> 15:51.270
<b>But still... sectionalism 
and lack of imagination.</b>

15:51.270 --> 15:54.340
<b>Not only are they not using 
the lessons we've learned in the east,</b>

15:54.340 --> 15:57.650
<b>they're punishing their most 
talented, loyal soldiers.</b>

15:57.650 --> 15:59.730
<b>I just don't think that...</b>

15:59.980 --> 16:02.480
<b>Don't say that, Lieutenant Colonel.</b>

16:02.480 --> 16:06.870
<b>This isn't meant as an apology, 
but there's talk of giving you all medals.</b>

16:06.870 --> 16:08.860
<b>Look forward to it.</b>

16:08.860 --> 16:11.500
<b>While I appreciate it,</b>

16:11.500 --> 16:15.370
<b>a bunch of pity medals on my chest 
won't do me any good.</b>

16:15.370 --> 16:17.100
<b>That's right...</b>

16:17.100 --> 16:22.500
<b>I'd prefer to end the war and brag 
to my children about our victory.</b>

16:22.500 --> 16:25.460
<b>Are you thinking of marrying, Colonel?</b>

16:25.460 --> 16:28.820
<b>There was talk of it before the war.</b>

16:28.820 --> 16:32.610
<b>Once the war's over, of course 
I'm going to think about it.</b>

16:32.610 --> 16:34.500
<b>I see...</b>

16:34.990 --> 16:38.830
<b>Either way, we'll want to 
end this war somehow.</b>

16:38.830 --> 16:43.090
<b>I've been promised that if it works out,
I can live off royalties after the war.</b>

16:43.420 --> 16:45.270
<b>Live off royalties?</b>

16:45.270 --> 16:49.310
<b>General Rudersdorf has promised 
to make a picture book about me.</b>

16:49.310 --> 16:50.840
<b>A picture book?</b>

16:50.840 --> 16:52.310
<b>The general said that?</b>

16:52.310 --> 16:56.420
<b>I'll be the hero. 
He's promised to give it his all.</b>

16:56.420 --> 16:58.820
<b>Don't you think that 
would be interesting?</b>

16:59.760 --> 17:02.540
<b>That would be pretty funny.</b>

17:02.540 --> 17:05.840
<b>Buy me a cup of coffee 
when the checks start coming in.</b>

17:06.040 --> 17:07.660
<b>Yes, of course.</b>

17:09.640 --> 17:12.190
<b><i>And while I'm thinking about 
what comes next...</i></b>

17:17.880 --> 17:19.890
<b><i>No, I don't have time to think!</i></b>

17:19.890 --> 17:22.290
<b><i>This is exactly like when 
you work at a black company</i></b>

17:22.290 --> 17:24.760
<b><i>and don't have time to think 
about finding a new job!</i></b>

17:24.760 --> 17:26.890
<b><i>What do I do?</i></b>

17:26.890 --> 17:28.360
<b>Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff!</b>

17:29.580 --> 17:31.360
<b>General Romel!</b>

17:31.360 --> 17:34.620
<b>I owe you one, Lieutenant Colonel.</b>

17:42.560 --> 17:45.590
<b>Sir, don't you think 
you've had enough to drink?</b>

17:46.070 --> 17:48.730
<b>There's no focus in the capital.</b>

17:48.730 --> 17:51.410
<b>I can't even breathe the air 
unless I'm drunk.</b>

17:53.380 --> 17:55.590
<b>Where is reality?</b>

17:55.590 --> 17:58.370
<b>Where the hell's the exit to reality?</b>

17:58.370 --> 18:01.030
<b>That's what everybody back from 
the front lines really thinks.</b>

18:01.030 --> 18:05.910
<b>We get blamed for not delivering
the fantasies of people in the rear.</b>

18:05.910 --> 18:07.890
<b>It's ridiculous.</b>

18:09.910 --> 18:12.460
<b>People only see what they want to see.</b>

18:12.460 --> 18:14.640
<b>They only discover what 
they want to discover.</b>

18:15.180 --> 18:19.240
<b>And it's the same for 
General Rudersdorf, I think!</b>

18:20.740 --> 18:22.200
<b>Lieutenant Colonel!</b>

18:23.730 --> 18:27.750
<b>Don't think that what you can see 
is everything there is.</b>

18:42.490 --> 18:45.220
<b>I've heard reports of your successes.</b>

18:49.680 --> 18:52.320
<b>The situation's not good.</b>

18:52.740 --> 18:56.900
<b>I believe we've at least 
stopped the bleeding, though.</b>

18:57.930 --> 19:02.800
<b>Zettour's shored up our defenses in 
the east. It's no longer good or bad.</b>

19:03.210 --> 19:05.280
<b>Has there been some change 
in the war situation?</b>

19:06.530 --> 19:10.580
<b>The High Leadership has a dream.</b>

19:10.580 --> 19:13.130
<b>A dream?</b>

19:13.130 --> 19:17.790
<b>Dreams of new territory 
and a fortune in war reparations.</b>

19:18.060 --> 19:22.420
<b>We've shed too much blood in the war, 
and they want to make up for that.</b>

19:22.420 --> 19:25.450
<b>It's hard to believe they live 
in the same world we do.</b>

19:25.450 --> 19:29.320
<b>Shouldn't we be thinking about how 
we persuade the people back home?</b>

19:29.320 --> 19:32.270
<b>Are you saying the military 
should get involved in politics?</b>

19:32.880 --> 19:35.560
<b>As things stand,
 I believe we have no choice.</b>

19:35.560 --> 19:39.810
<b>If you want to talk politics, 
do it after you leave the military.</b>

19:40.370 --> 19:42.760
<b>If you're willing to let me quit,</b>

19:42.760 --> 19:45.790
<b>I'll become a civilian and start 
running for parliament today.</b>

19:45.790 --> 19:49.280
<b>But it seems you know 
little about politics.</b>

19:49.280 --> 19:52.220
<b>There's a minimum age to run.</b>

19:52.220 --> 19:53.700
<b>Or did you not know that?</b>

19:53.700 --> 19:55.570
<b>Apologies.</b>

19:55.570 --> 19:59.840
<b>My elders seem to be making a giant mess 
of everything, so I couldn't help myself.</b>

20:01.950 --> 20:03.970
<b>The reality is that we're doomed.</b>

20:08.980 --> 20:13.410
<b>General, we have a duty to say 
what we have to say!</b>

20:15.230 --> 20:21.800
<b>The High Leadership is beginning serious 
discussions about conquering Ildoa.</b>

20:21.800 --> 20:24.430
<b>Ildoa? Conquering?</b>

20:24.430 --> 20:26.930
<b>They say that if we can remove 
the threat to the south,</b>

20:26.930 --> 20:33.620
<b>we can move a great deal of our forces 
from the south to the east.</b>

20:33.620 --> 20:34.890
<b>That's crazy.</b>

20:34.890 --> 20:37.770
<b>If we can't take out Ildoa 
in a single blow,</b>

20:37.770 --> 20:40.570
<b>the southern theater forces 
will be caught in a quagmire.</b>

20:40.570 --> 20:43.360
<b>And even if we succeeded in 
a strategic surprise attack...</b>

20:46.860 --> 20:51.990
<b><i>Are the Ildoans ready to fight a war, 
mentally or from a supply standpoint?</i></b>

20:51.990 --> 20:56.470
<b><i>Oh no... from an operations standpoint, 
we might actually be able to pull it off.</i></b>

20:56.470 --> 20:59.100
<b><i>Strategically, it's the dumbest thing 
we could possibly do, but...</i></b>

21:03.620 --> 21:06.420
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, 
they're simply looking into it.</b>

21:06.790 --> 21:11.000
<b>If there's no hope of it working, we can 
simply explain that to the leadership.</b>

21:11.480 --> 21:13.280
<b>Don't worry too much.</b>

21:13.950 --> 21:17.310
<b>But we also want a way 
to survive this war.</b>

21:17.800 --> 21:22.330
<b>It'd be nice if Ildoa could 
finally start being useful.</b>

22:55.040 --> 22:59.970
<b>Even if Ildoa was paying, 
I still might've bought too much.</b>

23:00.700 --> 23:04.070
<b>If the Lieutenant Colonel 
sees this stuffed rucksack...</b>

23:04.070 --> 23:06.820
<b>You bought way too much!</b>

23:06.820 --> 23:08.980
<b>Don't waste other people's money!</b>

23:08.980 --> 23:10.950
<b>I-I'm so sorry!</b>

23:11.720 --> 23:13.630
<b>Lieutenant Serebryakov...</b>

23:17.110 --> 23:21.630
<b>I wish today wasn't our last day 
in Ildoa, don't you?</b>

23:21.630 --> 23:23.870
<b>Y-Yeah...</b>

23:26.080 --> 23:27.460
<b>What's wrong?</b>

23:27.460 --> 23:29.740
<b>No, nothing...</b>

23:29.740 --> 23:30.830
<b>I see.</b>

23:30.830 --> 23:34.390
<b>Now, let's go back to our beloved Empire!</b>

23:34.760 --> 23:35.600
<b>Right!</b>

23:37.010 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time
A Way to Survive</b>
